From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:43:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] utl, gpl, rsz, grt: options structs shared by C++, Tcl and
 Python

OpenROAD #11755 (RFC, draft) at 1bdd0d53cd, rebased onto bazel-orfs's
OpenROAD pin and the carries before this one: global_placement,
repair_design and global_route take their settings as an options struct
declared once in C++, as generated switches and as `-options dict`, with
the old switch names kept as aliases.

What the rebase added to the RFC, for what the pin and the carries have
that its base did not: gpl's power group, macro_area_in_denominator and
clusters_file; grt's backing_file and incremental, optional so that the
route embedded in global_placement leaves the router's state alone;
findResizeSlacks takes both repair_design and placed_net; global_route
-unguided_only stays a switch of the Tcl command. The pin clamps
virtual_cts.max_skew_fraction with a warning, so the RFC's range check on
it is dropped. Its CMake changes are dropped, CMake being gone.

Not upstreamed: the RFC is open. Carried for the comparison with ORFS
#4771's command arguments grammar; not proposed for merge.
